eing told the doc is red.","why":"All Stop hooks run on the same stop event, so DOC_STOP ran in that first event with stop_hook_active=false and exited 2 with the message (src/main.rs:534-538) before the pass at src/main.rs:535; a router never edits docs (DEC-30, docs/decisions/router.html:23); Keel's .claude/settings.json:78-87 has one Stop hook."},{"location":"scripts/router-worker.sh:846","claim":"A DEAD spawn leaves a brief copy and a run dir with no session file, which prune never clears, contrary to its contract.","why":"prune's contract is 'brief copies of sessions no longer listed' (scripts/router-worker.sh:30-32, DEC-44 docs/decisions/router.html:91) and a DEAD spawn records no session (seal :210 with empty sid, :850-852); a DEAD with rc=0 (:839) may be listed later and still read the copy; the copy is self-ignored (:128) and goes with the worktree."},{"location":"scripts/router-worker.sh:360","claim":"close_lines adds a third 'is merged' rule unlike worktree remove and router-watch.sh check_merged, so a fast-forward merged branch never shows under Close.","why":"Listing only branches merged --no-ff is deliberate: docs/decisions/router.html:98 (DEC-45 W7 Close block) and the comment at scripts/router-worker.sh:357-358; the differing tests at scripts/router-worker.sh:522 and scripts/router-watch.sh:104-110 answer other questions."},{"location":"scripts/router-worker.sh:370","claim":"The Close block's rev-list plus awk never exits early, so each watchdog tick costs output growing with every merge on the base since the branch merged.","why":"rev-list --ancestry-path walks the whole range before printing, so an early awk exit would not shorten it; the cost is the same order as merge-base --is-ancestor at scripts/router-worker.sh:522 and scripts/router-watch.sh:106, once per worktree per 5-minute tick, until the worktree is removed (:375)."}],"nits":[{"location":"src/main.rs:1103","finding":"The unit test doc_stop_tells_the_router_once_and_holds_every_other_sess